WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.290
<i>No!</i>

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.460
You can't even do <i>this</i>?!

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.470
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.210
Wait, old lady—I mean, Sensei!

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.880
Please teach me ballet!

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.980
Act 4: "I Can Do Ballet Now"

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.980
I'm sorry I didn't come to class!

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.650
Idiot!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.860
When have you ever seen a prince 
with a shaved head?!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.870
Wh-What?!

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.250
I didn't think about that!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.780
I can tell!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.310
Also, here.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.620
It's a box of sweets and monthly tuition...

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.610
My mother told me to bring them.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.630
Ballet?

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.630
You should do it.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.880
Huh?!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.190
I knew already. Your sister told me.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.630
And I know your dad is pleased

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.250
that you thought about what 
he said for eight years.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:48.280
Okay.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.390
Stand in fifth position.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:51.820
Like a prince.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.390
Oh? You look like a very dignified prince.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.000
Are you visualizing something?

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.040
Char.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.560
Usually someone replies with a dancer's name.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.630
You know,

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.260
I don't really care about being a prince, 
and I've got a shaved head, too.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.240
I'd rather dance as Rothbart.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.640
I don't understand why Luou's so 
hung up about being the prince...

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.220
Ma'am.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.810
The "danseur noble."

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.690
That's what a dancer who's qualified 
to take on the prince's part is called.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.200
The "prince" is a kind of pinnacle.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.630
To dance the part of the prince,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.290
you need a certain physical 
appearance, skill, acting ability,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.960
charisma, musicality, grace, 
and support ability.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.330
Only someone who has all those qualities

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.710
is allowed to play the part of the prince.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.030
It's territory that can't be 
reached by hard work alone.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.600
If I become the prince, will I only 
be able to dance that part?

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.600
Didn't you hear what I said? It's a pinnacle.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.730
If you're able to dance as the prince 
and also master character roles,

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.050
then you can dance any part.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.770
Well, but it would impossible for you 
to dance the part of the prince

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.990
at a top company in Russia, 
the nation of ballet.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.990
Oh?

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.000
That's what I'll do, then.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:35.830
Huh?

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.070
I said,

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.090
I'll become a danseur noble in Russia.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.390
Bold talk for a kid with a shaved head!

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.480
I'm serious about this!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.120
H-Hey! Don't laugh, old lady!

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.680
Wow, what's that?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.450
Murao!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.990
Don't run—or jump—in the halls!

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.710
What <i>is</i> that, anyway? What are you doing?!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.530
Coupé-jeté en tournant!

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.990
It's ballet!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.080
He's so damn loud.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.590
<i>I can't stop!</i>

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.500
<i>If I stop...</i>

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.220
<i>I'll die!</i>

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.510
<i>I...</i>

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.230
<i>can do ballet now!</i>

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.350
I'll become a danseur noble in Russia.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.290
Bold talk for a kid with a shaved head!

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.110
I'm serious about this!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.110
What a foolish pipe dream!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.620
At the top ballet schools in Russia,

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.960
the nation of ballet,

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.030
only about 30 boys are accepted 
out of thousands who apply.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.800
In addition, for the next eight years, 
exams weed them out between levels,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.630
and less than half are left by graduation.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.980
After that,

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:09.180
only a handful of dancers are able to 
join world-class ballet companies

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.050
like the Mariinsky or Bolshoi companies.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.550
For a Japanese man to
 become danseur noble there

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.430
is like a dream within a dream.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.020
Seriously?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.900
I can't believe you'd say that after 
taking lessons for barely a month.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.450
Really, it's crazy.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:30.160
The first time you danced here,

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:36.330
I also saw the same pipe dream for you!

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.310
Right?

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.700
Hold on to the barre.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:53.480
Huh?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.430
Point your toes.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.950
You really have amazing foot structure.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.630
You have long arms and legs. 
And long fingers, too.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.690
You have big feet and a high instep, 
which is good for ballet.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.450
And a small head and long neck.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.520
Plus, your face...

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.550
isn't too bad, when you don't talk.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:16.660
You actually have what it takes to go pro.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.240
But that's all just what I look like.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.920
Oh? Ballet mainly depends 
on the raw material.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.800
You must have a silhouette suited for ballet.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.550
The only part of your body 
I'm concerned about...

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.890
is your height.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.470
Nah, I'll be fine!

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.350
My dad was tall!

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.800
You were probably always very athletic,

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:46.270
but your core strength and flexibility are
 probably thanks to Jeet Kune Do, right?

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.520
It makes me want to thank 
your Jeet Kune Do teacher.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:56.110
<i>I need to go apologize 
properly to Uncle Mioka.</i>

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.420
Oh, I'm so glad!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.410
Huh? About what?

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:15.250
I thought you weren't going 
to do ballet anymore.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:20.450
I couldn't sort out my feelings,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.390
and it made me sulky. Sorry about that.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.900
<i>Uh... Huh?</i>

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.900
Uh, well... not about that...

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.900
<i>Was I just being used?</i>

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.820
Y-You can feel it if you want.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.870
The short hair's pretty fun to touch.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.060
<i>Ballet...</i>

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.920
<i>is the best!</i>

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.560
How ridiculous.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.940
Okay, Miyako, practice 
the choreography for Swan Lake.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.660
Jumpei, continue your barre work.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.390
What? Again?!

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:10.020
I did barre work all day yesterday, too!

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.520
It's less than two months 
until the performance, right?

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.440
You can move on once you can 
do the barre work properly.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.530
You don't do barre on stage!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:22.080
I've already learned 
the prince's choreography!

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:38.340
As usual, I wouldn't call 
that ballet. It's an eyesore.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.300
For example, with your pirouette...

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.070
You're not turning out enough, 
so you're crooked going in,

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:47.100
and end up using brute force to turn.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.290
What? Really?!

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.980
Try turning while focusing 
on keeping your turnout.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.110
Don't let it go for even an instant.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.490
<i>Turning's easy.</i>

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>I don't think something like that 
would make a difference.</i>

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:11.170
See? You can't even complete one turn.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.340
What?! No way!

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.100
If you want to do ballet,

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.590
you're not allowed to dance 
whatever you want anymore.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:24.220
Th-That one just now didn't
 count. One more time!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.230
You're crooked.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:28.650
What? It was just a little...

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.020
Isn't it fine as long as I can turn?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.100
It's not fine.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.320
It's not just turns.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.280
All of ballet uses a set of basic movements,

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.610
and even difficult techniques are
 just applications of the basics.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.760
If you don't get rid of the bad habits you 
picked up while dancing on your own

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.000
and nail down the correct,
 basic movements,

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.030
then what you're doing 
can't be called "ballet."

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.430
For those like Miyako and Luou,

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:56.250
who have had the basics drilled 
into them since they were young,

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.700
ballet movements have become 
part of their bodies.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:03.720
There are more than ten years 
between them and your bad habits.

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.820
Incorrect movements will lead to injury, too.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.350
Doesn't your knee hurt?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.630
No, it doesn't!

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.400
What's with that face?

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.410
Embarrassment and stubbornness 
are enemies of growth.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.550
So, what should you be doing right now?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.550
Hey, hey!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:25.660
Okay, now, ignore the boy 
who has to practice late.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.540
You're humming too loud!

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:33.330
Jumpei, don't join the class 
without permission!

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:35.330
Here.

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:36.920
These are full-soled shoes.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.110
These will help work the 
bottom of your feet more.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.780
Clean up and put the key in the mailbox.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:51.690
I can't move...

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:57.170
Hey, Chizuru-san, there's only a month left.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:59.190
Please teach me the choreography.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.950
I want to dance.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.660
I want to jump.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.820
I want to turn.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.030
Chizuru-san...

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.840
You can learn the choreography later.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.480
Once you've got the basics, 
the dance will come easily.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.470
Jumpei.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.840
Once the basics become second nature,

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.570
you'll be able to dance more freely.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.920
Luou-kun, you didn't eat dinner, did you?

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:31.350
You're just eating junk food, aren't you?

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:36.230
Oh, your grandmother sent a postcard.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.610
What about your contract with me?

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:52.860
Bor-ing, te-di-ous, 
ne-ver-end-ing barre work...

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:56.620
<i>This is like being forced into a ballet mold.</i>

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.040
<i>Dancing more freely instead 
of dancing the way I want to...</i>

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.440
<i>What the heck?</i>

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:08.170
<i>How far does that mean I can go?</i>

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.640
84-453-3-7-8 Asugaya-nantou,
Suginami-ku, Tokyo
 To: Mori Luou c/o Godai 
Home hinemosu 3-chome, 
Kuragamauji, Kanagawa

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:15.300
Luou, you want to study abroad at an overseas
 ballet school under famous teachers.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:19.150
To do that, you need to dance in overseas 
competitions and get a scholarship.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.640
Right?

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.890
In exchange for arranging for you 
to enter overseas competitions,

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:27.610
I gave you two conditions:

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:33.040
go to school and win MVP 
at the ballet festival.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.210
To do that, you need 
to participate in lesso—

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.240
I...

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:40.430
don't think I can study under you, after all.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.410
I can't bear to stand on the same 
stage as that wild monkey.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:50.050
<i>He</i> wants to be a Bolshoi or
 Mariinsky danseur noble?

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:51.720
How ridiculous!

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.180
You don't like it?

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:01.540
Didn't your grandmother want 
the same thing for you?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.000
Mazuru could do it in one try!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.460
Mazuru could do it more beautifully!

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.670
Mazuru could...

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.400
The key to the studio?

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.930
It's not on the dresser?

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.390
Maybe someone stayed late.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:37.570
The mailbox, then...

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.550
Huh? It's not there.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.950
Luou?!

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:52.250
Oh, is this the music from <i>Don Quixote</i>?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.270
Jumpei?!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.620
You can't dance without permission!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.480
Miyako, he's just doing barre work.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.030
Jumpei?!

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.000
Was he doing this all night?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.960
There's no way, right?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.160
They're worn out.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.920
No way! That's impossible!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.410
He hasn't even had those shoes for a month.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.390
It wasn't just one night...

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.930
They wouldn't have ended up like that 
unless he's been dancing every night.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.420
Oh, welcome back. I'm leaving now.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:14.450
Oh, my. This is when you've been leaving?

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:19.200
I was just thinking that when I wake up, 
all I'm left with is a ton of laundry.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.620
My teacher keeps nagging me about 
sleeping at least four hours a night,

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.920
so I'm home then.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.210
I know it's summer vacation, 
but is this really okay?

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.550
It's fine.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.170
When I hear the music, I don't need to sleep.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.770
It wasn't you I was worried about.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.030
Ever since you were little,

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.510
you never slept much. I never
 knew what to do with you.

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:42.240
But aren't you causing trouble for your teacher?

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.900
Mom, you look... older...

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:49.080
You don't have to stay 
with me the whole time.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.650
It'd be a waste if you practiced 
the movements wrong.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.410
Well, I guess it's about time 
you tried the pas de deux.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.220
Yes! Finally!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.370
I already know the choreography!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:08.210
I've been watching you two dancing it!

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:10.820
Okay, then, why don't you try it?

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.320
Okay, music start.

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:25.070
You come to the lake to hunt swans for fun,

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:30.060
but instead of a swan, a girl 
appears, and she's your type.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.400
"Type"?

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:39.380
That's it. Jumpei, don't get embarrassed.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.430
You're the prince, after all.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:45.770
You're full of curiosity. 
You're innocent and confident.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:48.050
You don't know what it means 
for people to dislike you.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.010
You're a 14-year-old prince.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.850
<i>Oh, man!</i>

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:55.430
<i>What is this?</i>

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:56.940
<i>What are you?</i>

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:02.070
<i>This sound of premonition... won't go away!</i>

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:05.240
<i>Hey, tell me.</i>

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.690
<i>Tell me a secret you've never 
told anyone else before.</i>

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:16.200
<i>Look, it's like the world is changing 
from where we touch.</i>

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.290
<i>Tell me.</i>

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:32.290
<i>What'll happen if I touch you more?</i>

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:33.420
That's enough.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.800
Wow, you really do know the choreography.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.570
Your acting was very good, too.

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.910
<i>Well, I'm not sure I was acting...</i>

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:45.850
Miyako, you seemed to be 
put off by the excited prince,

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.640
but that naïveté was fine, too.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.160
Wha—

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.170
"Put off"...

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.690
It wasn't that I was put off!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.650
I was just... surprised...

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.860
But you forgot the basics!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.840
Your fingers were sloppy, 
and you didn't pull up your knees.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:02.200
That's what happens when you 
cram everything in so fast.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.520
For the upcoming performance,

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:07.700
prioritize getting the fine positioning
 right, instead of the acting.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.740
You'll be compared when 
dancing with Luou especially,

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:13.030
and the flaws in your dancing will stand out.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.340
When is he going to come to practice?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:25.550
<i>Of course, he's probably avoiding me...</i>

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.030
Oh, you're here!

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.170
Hey, wait a minute!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.600
You know the part where Rothbart 
and the prince dance together?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.060
Do it with me.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.670
I'll go home after that.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.870
Oh, this is when they're fighting, right?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.890
You'll dance in the festival, right?

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.270
Whoa...

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:20.670
Was there a move like that 
in the choreography?

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.830
Go home, wild monkey.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.150
Hey...

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:31.570
Why did you dance in the gym?

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.430
It's amazing, you know?

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.120
You've got like, a fan club now,

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.930
and the video from it is super popular.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:41.930
Everything changed because
 of that whole thing!

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.460
Nothing's changed.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:50.490
Those guys lost interest in me 
because you distracted them.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:51.680
What?!

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:55.690
Were you trying to force your 
sickening "justice" on me?

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:58.310
It would've been better if they'd 
just kept making fun of me!

00:20:58.310 --> 00:20:59.820
That's not it!

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.570
That's not it at all!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:05.180
Your dancing actually reached them, too!

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:10.200
At least, I was able to tell them back then...

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.930
and I'm here right now because...

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:20.160
Because when you danced, 
it ended up changing my life!

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:23.970
That's why, you bastard...

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.970
In other words, um...

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.050
Thanks.

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:39.260
Anyway, I said what I wanted to say,

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.600
so I'm gonna go now!

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.040
Oh, one more thing.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:49.010
It's true that I'm a wild monkey 
compared to you,

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:51.330
and I'm knee-deep in basic training.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.720
But you know,

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.670
while you keep hiding in your room,

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.100
I'm gonna get better than you.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.890
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:37.020
Odette!

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:41.150
The first girl I chose myself, 
disobeying the queen!

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.690
I wanted to be faithful to you!

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.940
<i>Dance Dance Danseur</i>, Act 5: "I Can't Die"!

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:49.900
Act 5 
"I Can't Die"
